  "notes": [
    "dist = exact shortest proof length in Isomer's action space (ADR-003): fresh and consumed variable values come from the problem pool (theory constants, skolems occurring in lhs/rhs, subterms of lhs/rhs of size <= pool_max_size = 3); term size <= max(|lhs|,|rhs|)+6. The action space is symmetric, so bidirectional BFS distances are exact. dist is null when the labeller stopped first.",
    "eval and held-out problems (test_depth, test_deep, test_theory) were labelled with 20000 expansions, 20x the largest recommended benchmark budget (1000), and a cap of 1500000 stored nodes; label_stop says which limit ended the search. Train and test_id were labelled with 3000 expansions and contain only problems bidirectional BFS solved within that budget with dist <= 4.",
    "test_deep holds eval problems with no exact dist. Grade them by the certified lower bound dist_lb (proven from completed BFS layers), never by dist_ub.",
    "dist_ub = length of the best known proof (the BFS proof if found, else the random walk). Walks that leave the size cap are rejected at generation, so dist_lb <= dist <= dist_ub always holds.",
    "every stored proof was accepted by the trusted kernel at build time."
